## Git Workflow

### Commit Standards
- **Descriptive commit messages** - explain what and why
- **Sequential commits** - commit each logical phase separately
- **Test before commit** - ensure `cargo check` passes
- **Update documentation** - include plan updates in commits

### Branch Management
- **Main branch**: Production-ready code
- **Feature branches**: Use for major feature development
- **Merge carefully**: Always review and test before merging

## Common Patterns

### Module Organization
```rust
// In mod.rs files
pub mod module_name;
pub use module_name::*; // For convenient re-exports
```

### Error Handling
```rust
use crate::agent::core::AgentError;

// Use appropriate error variants
AgentError::Other(format!("Description: {}", details))
AgentError::ToolError("Tool-specific error".to_string())
```

### Async Patterns
```rust
use async_trait::async_trait;

#[async_trait]
pub trait TraitName: Send + Sync {
    async fn method_name(&self) -> Result<Type, AgentError>;
}
```

## Testing Strategy

### Required Tests
- **Unit tests** for individual components
- **Integration tests** for agent interactions
- **Compilation tests** via `cargo check`
- **End-to-end workflows** for user scenarios

### Test Organization
```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_specific_functionality() {
        // Test implementation
    }
}
```

